## 6. Full working example (copy-paste)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>MapLibre fly-to demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet"/>
  <style>
    body,html{margin:0;height:100%}
    #map{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;width:100%}
    .control{
      position:absolute;top:10px;left:10px;
      background:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);
      padding:6px 10px;border-radius:4px;
      font-family:sans-serif;cursor:pointer;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<div class="control" id="flyBtn">Fly to Paris</div>

<script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://demotiles.maplibre.org/style.json',
    center: [-0.1276, 51.5074],
    zoom: 10
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // optional marker so the user sees the target
    new maplibregl.Marker({color:'#ff6600'})
      .setLngLat([2.3522, 48.8566])
      .addTo(map);

    document.getElementById('flyBtn')
      .addEventListener('click', () => {
        map.flyTo({
          center: [2.3522, 48.8566],
          zoom: 12,
          bearing: 30,
          pitch: 45,
          duration: 2000,
          curve: 1.5,
          easing: t => t,
          essential: true
        });
      });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Open the file in a browser, click **Fly to Paris**, and watch the camera lift, rotate, and settle on the city with a smooth 2-second animation.

---

## 7. Quick checklist (cartographic sanity)

| ✅ Item | Why it matters |
|--------|----------------|
| **Halo on labels** (`rgba(0,0,0,0.75)` for imagery) | Guarantees legibility over unpredictable photo backgrounds. |
| **`essential: true`** | Respects users who have “reduce motion” turned on (the map will jump instantly). |
| **`duration` ≤ 3000 ms** | Long enough to be perceived as a movement, short enough not to stall interaction. |
| **`pitch` ≤ 60°** | Keeps the map readable; extreme tilt can hide labels behind terrain shading. |
| **Button contrast** (≥ 4.5:1) | WCAG AA compliance for the UI element that triggers the animation. |
| **Layer order** – keep your data layers **below** the basemap’s symbol layers (see the *injection pattern* in the skill) | Prevents your geometry from covering important place-name labels. |

Follow those points and you’ll have a smooth, accessible, and cartographically sound fly-to experience in MapLibre GL JS. Happy mapping!
